//
// Doc 31 R1, the host-only half: ffn_resident's dataflow, INTERPRETED OUT
// OF THE BUILT MODULE.
//
// The resident FFN interior moves every byte through hand-derived patterns
// (the w_up packing, the shim's row-major->blocked retile, the strided
// chunk extraction, the w_down refill, a global K order assembled from
// three herds' loops and three segment-scope feed nests).
// builders/test_ffn_resident.py BUILDS build_ffn_resident_module and
// executes the resulting air.ir.Module in numpy -- every air.dma_memcpy_nd
// and air.channel.put/get with the offsets, sizes and strides the op
// actually carries, every scf.for at its actual bounds, every func.call
// dispatched by the symbol the builder named, the three herds as four
// concurrent actors each -- f64 throughout, and requires the composition to
// equal gelu(hidden @ w_up) @ w_down to f64 round-off.
//
// `[2026-08-12]` REBUILT, queue item 17. Until today this arm imported
// ffn_resident_pack_w_up and NEVER BUILT THE MODULE: it re-derived every
// DMA pattern and every loop order by hand, so the builder and the check
// were two independent transcriptions of one design and the check could
// only ever disagree with itself. Re-imposing the exact c-major w_down
// order route E1 deleted still printed 5/5. Measured after the rebuild, on
// the real pre-E1 builder source (918c202f, unmodified, loaded and built):
// the shipped builder emits THREE textual segment-scope refills and comes
// out element-exact at 5.457e-12; the pre-E1 builder emits SIX -- four of
// them landing in the same L2 buffer -- and comes out at 4.72e+03. The
// in-arm negative control reproduces that figure to the digit.
//
// This arm is deliberately the one that stays LIVE while the operator's
// device gate (run_npu2_ffn_resident_peano.lit) is parked on wall 6: no
// aircc, no XRT, no kernel objects, no NPU. It reads the AIR module, so it
// models addressing and delivery ORDER and nothing else -- not timing, not
// BD folding, not channel fusion, and neither wall 5's D1 nor wall 6's
// lock-conservation imbalance (queue item 18). Cite it for the dataflow;
// the device gate settles the rest.
//
// THIS RECIPE AND THE SCRIPT ARE ONE ARM, and that is stated rather than
// worked around. There is no `make` target for it and none should be added:
// a second name for one command is exactly what let a gate list "run the
// script" and "run the lit" as two steps and call the arm doubly covered
// (queue item 17). What the recipe adds over `python3 builders/
// test_ffn_resident.py` is the assertions below -- that the two negative
// controls FIRED and were rejected, that the census is live, and that the
// count is what it claims. Run the recipe, not the script (doc 23 section
// 5). No framework dependency: pytest is not in the sandbox venv, so the
// file runs as a plain script and prints a named pass count.
//
// RUN: python3 %S/builders/test_ffn_resident.py | FileCheck %s
//
// Element-exactness, checked as an ORDER of magnitude rather than a digit:
// the mantissa moves with the BLAS, the exponent does not. e-1x is at or
// under 1e-10 against operands of order 1e+2, which is f64 round-off.
// CHECK: module-interpreted dataflow: max |y - reference| = {{[0-9.]+}}e-1{{[0-9]}} over 64x768 f64 elements
//
// Liveness, so the exactness line cannot pass vacuously: the interpreter
// must have dispatched the kernels the design derives (768 = 4*4*24 up +
// 4*96 down in-place accumulates, 20 zeros = 16 up groups + 4 guarded
// first-K-step calls, 96 GeLU chunks), moved every channel op, and drained
// every staged stream the shim delivered.
// CHECK: dispatch census: ffn_gelu_bf16 96, ffn_matmul_bf16_bf16_up_proj 768, ffn_zero_bf16_up_proj 20
// CHECK: channel census: ffn_res_down_feed 768p/768g, ffn_res_g 96p/96g, ffn_res_h 96p/96g, ffn_res_up_feed 768p/768g; undrained staged streams: 0
//
// THE NEGATIVE CONTROLS ARE MATCHED HERE, both of them, because an arm that
// cannot fail is not a gate -- the lesson of queue items 10, 14 and 17 in
// one week. Each must report an error of order 1 or larger against a bar of
// 1e-9. A control that stopped being re-imposed would print no line and
// this recipe would go red; a control that stopped discriminating would
// print an e-1x figure and the e+0x match would fail.
// CHECK: negative control: c-major w_down refill (pre-E1 c unroll) -> max err {{[0-9.]+}}e+0{{[0-9]}}
// CHECK: negative control: hidden 4-D retile walked with its two inner strides swapped -> max err {{[0-9.]+}}e+0{{[0-9]}}
//
// `[2026-08-12]` 8 -> 10, queue item 21 (wall 7). Clause 9 asserts the down
// feed's H staging is one L2 allocation PER GeLU COLUMN, and control 3 is its
// matched refusal. This is not style: model (M2) at the head of the test module
// assumes an L2 staging buffer's values "land in the order the shim issued
// them", and with ONE shared allocation at herd_x > 1 that assumption is FALSE
// on hardware -- air-to-aie emits one S2MM channel per GeLU core onto one
// single-slot memtile buffer, all on the same counting semaphore with the same
// acquire/release counts, so the write order is an arbitration outcome. This
// arm interprets AIR and therefore cannot see that; without clause 9 it
// certifies element-exact a module the device answers wrong. The control is
// what makes the clause able to fail: it rebuilds the shared form
// (`shared_h_staging=True`) and requires it REFUSED.
// CHECK: negative control: shared H staging (wall 7's form) -> REFUSED
//
// The count last, matched exactly so a clause that stops being defined
// fails here rather than passing quietly.
// CHECK: ffn_resident emulation tests: 10/10 passed
